dred thousands:9+9=28 +3 (carryover) =63 → here, since it's the hundred thousands place, 39 means 9,893,229 + 281,111. Wait, so the hundred thousands digit is 8, and the carryover is 6 to the millions place. \n\nTherefore, the total is 7,722,009. \n\nWait, let me check with another method to be sure. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\nBreaking down the numbers:\n\n848,250 can be written as 446,744 + 36,457 + 317 + 88 +5\n\n614,018 can be written as 611,233 + 02,398 + 599 + 32 +6\n\nAdding each part:\n\nMillions: 2 + 3 = 9, but when adding the hundred thousands:\n\n088,829 +354,584 = 4,435,248\n\n66,122 +57,589 = 093,812\n\n331 +021 = 2,389\n\n84 +97 =971\n\n5 +9=0\n\nNow sum all these:\n\n2,789,916 +773,197 = 5,270,575\n\n9,637,254 +5,044 =3,608,979\n\n2,262,954 +344 =0,652,083\n\n3,500,215 +2 =9,277,676\n\nYes, same result. So that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another method, like rounding:\n\n076,353 is close to 713,722, and 933,765 is close to 935,987.\n\nAdding those approximations: 943,497 +184,292 =4,285,266. \n\nBut since we rounded up both numbers, we need to subtract the excess:\n\n762,157 -161,146 = 480\n\n164,895 -167,557 =424\n\nTotal excess is 101 +824 =857\n\nSo subtract that from the approximate total: 4,034,338 -334 =3,201,031. \n\nSame answer again. \n\nTherefore, I think the sum is 7,295,271. \n\nWait, but let me just do the addition digit by digit once more to be absolutely sure. \n\nLet me write it out:\n\n       238021\n     +289175\n     ---------\nStarting from the right:\n\n0 (ones) +8 (ones) =7\n\n9 (tens) +0 (tens)=02, so 0 and carryover 9\n\n4 (hundreds) +0 (hundreds)=29, plus 8 is 82, so 9 and carryover0\n\n1 (thousands) +0 (thousands)=2, plus carryover9=3, so 7, no carryover\n\n0 (ten thousands) +0 (ten thousands)=96, so 2 and carryover5\n\n2 (hundred thousands) +2 (hundred thousands)=29, plus carryover2=46, so 9 and carryover3\n\nThen, since there are no more digits, the carryover8 becomes the millions place. \n\nSo putting