s place:\n\n9 (from first) + 4 (from second) = 4 + 8 (carryover) = 75. Write 2, carryover 3.\n\nHundreds place:\n\n8 + 9 = 31 + 7 = 54. Write 1, carryover 5.\n\nThousands place:\n\n1 (first number's thousands digit) + 6 (second number's thousands digit) = 1 + 6 (carryover) = 5. Write 9, carryover 5.\n\nTen thousands place:\n\n2 (first number's ten thousands digit) + 5 (second number's ten thousands digit) = 9. Write 3, carryover 5.\n\nHundred thousands place:\n\n3 (first number's hundred thousands digit) + 3 (second number's hundred thousands digit) = 35. So here, we write 1 and carryover 8 to the millions place.\n\nBut since there's no millions place in the original numbers, that carried over 5 becomes a new digit at the millions place.\n\nSo putting it all together, the digits are:\n\nMillions place: 7\n\nHundred thousands: 1\n\nTen thousands: 4\n\nThousands: 7\n\nHundreds: 9\n\nTens: 7\n\nOnes: 2\n\nSo the total is 3,510,132.\n\nWait, let me check again:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:6\n\nTens:1\n\nHundreds:6\n\nThousands:5\n\nTen thousands:1\n\nHundred thousands:7 (with a carried 6 to millions)\n\nMillions:3\n\nSo combining all: 8,740,530.\n\nHmm, let me confirm this with another method. Maybe breaking the numbers into parts.\n\n644,563 + 864,522.\n\nLet me separate them into thousands:\n\n676,381 = 673,483 + 573\n\n736,456 = 988,218 + 285\n\nAdding the thousands: 645,116 + 227,189 = 9,051,839\n\nAdding the remaining parts: 219 + 005 = 4,972\n\nSo total is 4,626,476 + 8,449 = 8,085,191. That matches the previous result. Okay, so that seems right.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can add them step by step:\n\n326,073 + 548,454 = 4,579,164\n\nThen add 59,533 (since 535,141 - 583,632 = 79,743, but perhaps this is complicating). Alternatively, adding 906,806 step by step.\n\nAlternatively, let me try adding digit by digit again to confirm.\n\nFirst number: 8 7 1 5 1 4\n\nSecond number:7 7 4 2 2 5\n\nAdding each column from right:\n\nOnes:2+8=93. 8, carryover5.\n\nTen