messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the sum of 942904 and 804851?', "<think>:\nOkay, so I need to find the sum of 814,352 and 467,160. Hmm, let me think about how to approach this. Both numbers are pretty large, so I should probably write them down to make sure I add each digit correctly. Let me start by aligning the numbers vertically by their place values. \n\nFirst, I'll write 480,711 on top and then 136,726 below it. Let me check the alignment:\n\n```\n  085425\n+ 089462\n---------\n```\n\nWait, actually, I should make sure that the digits are properly aligned by their place values. Let me confirm each digit's position. The rightmost digit is the units place, then tens, hundreds, thousands, ten thousands, hundred thousands, and so on. Let me write each number out with commas to see the places clearly:\n\n816,067 breaks down as:\n- 3 (hundred thousands)\n- 9 (ten thousands)\n- 0 (thousands)\n- 6 (hundreds)\n- 7 (tens)\n- 2 (units)\n\nAnd 962,616 breaks down as:\n- 5 (hundred thousands)\n- 3 (ten thousands)\n- 3 (thousands)\n- 6 (hundreds)\n- 4 (tens)\n- 8 (units)\n\nSo when adding, each column should be:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (units place):\n\n0 (from 667,755) + 0 (from 528,120) = 6. That's straightforward.\n\nNext column (tens place):\n\n8 + 3 = 9. Okay, that's easy too.\n\nNext column (hundreds place):\n\n1 + 1. Hmm, 7 + 1 is 86. Wait, so I need to write down 1 and carry over 9 to the next column.\n\nMoving to the thousands place:\n\n4 + 3. But remember the carried over 4? So that's 3 + 0 + 9 = 1. So 0 in the thousands place.\n\nNext is the ten thousands place:\n\n5 + 8 = 6. No carryover here.\n\nThen the hundred thousands place:\n\n5 + 1 = 91. Wait a second, that's another two-digit number. So here, I would write down 4 in the hundred thousands place and carry over 7 to the millions place. Since both original numbers don't have a millions digit, this carried over 4 becomes the millions place in the sum.\n\nPutting all