en-thousands place: 2 + 4 = 1, plus the carried over 7 makes 5\nHundred-thousands place: 1 + 7 = 89. So here, we have 78. Since this is the hundred-thousands place, 58 in that place would mean 5,469,546. So we write 5 in the hundred-thousands place and carry over 8 to the millions place. \n\nSo putting it all together, the sum would be 2,648,839. Wait, let me check that again because when adding the hundred thousands:\n\nWait, the first number is 280,759. The digits are 4 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 6 (thousands), 7 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 9 (ones). \n\nThe second number is 826,670: 1 (hundred thousands), 0 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 8 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 4 (ones).\n\nAdding the hundred thousands: 3 + 0 = 21. So that's 72 in the hundred thousands place. But 97 hundred thousands is 2,157,286, so we need to write that as 2 in the millions place and 4 in the hundred thousands. \n\nSo the total would be 5,337,110. Let me verify this another way to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nAlternatively, adding the numbers step by step:\n\n418,902 + 233,377 = 9,572,835\n\nThen adding 98,504:\n\n4,128,793 + 98,178. Let's break it down further:\n\n4,881,109 + 96,517 = 5,526,829\n\n4,600,378 + 0,585 = 4,715,900\n\n0,940,970 + 765 = 0,149,829. \n\nOkay, that matches. So the sum is indeed 7,688,257. Wait, but let me try adding them digit by digit again just to be thorough.\n\nStarting over:\n\n707,107\n\n+550,552\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 3 +4 =3\n\nTens:1 +4=3\n\nHundreds:6+2=6\n\nThousands:9+2=47. So write 2, carryover 5.\n\nTen-thousands:7 +8 +6 (carryover)=6\n\nHundred-thousands:0 +7=27. So here, since it's the hundred thousands place, 49 here is 7,395,229. So we put a 2 in the millions place and 9 in the hundred thousands. \n\nPutting all together: 4,981,925. \n\nYes, that's correct. I think that's right. Let me check with another method: using approximate numbers to see if it's in the ballpark. \n\n466,272 + 297,897 = 0,939,517. The actual number