usands digit) and 2 (from 913,348's ten-thousands digit). 0 + 1 = 47. So 0 with a carryover of 7 ✔️\nHundred-thousands place: 9 + 4 =75 plus the carried 5 is 69. So writing 2 and carrying over 3 to the millions place. So the total would be 2,990,284. \n\nWait, but when I add the hundred-thousands digits: 3 (from 060,284) and 9 (from 309,846). 1+0 is 08, plus the 2 carried over is 83. So the digits would be 7 (million) 5 (hundred thousand), 1 (ten thousand), 9 (thousand), 2 (hundred), 3 (ten), 3 (one). So yes, that makes 2,001,040. \n\nHmm, but let me do another check by adding in another way. Maybe breaking down the numbers:\n\n961,012 + 261,743.\n\nLet me split them into parts:\n\n150,574 = 063,578 + 48,134 + 9,896 + 745 + 72 + 4\n\n911,108 = 044,586 + 26,636 + 2 + 353 + 23 + 8\n\nAdding each part:\n\n148,181 + 258,382 = 0,881,845\n\n39,535 + 98,567 = 582,721\n\n3,597 + 5 = 5,458\n\n129 + 862 = 9,385\n\n61 + 46 = 231\n\n1 + 2 = 4\n\nNow add all these together:\n\n5,092,547 + 677,248 = 9,745,273\n\n2,885,339 + 0,242 = 6,399,865\n\n9,258,948 + 8,767 = 3,677,655\n\n5,053,961 + 518 = 6,744,716\n\n8,879,516 + 4 = 7,953,377.\n\nOkay, that matches the previous result. So that seems correct. Alternatively, maybe using another method like adding 215,103 + 365,454 first, then adding the remaining 97,038.\n\n371,595 + 625,939 = 5,230,172\n\nThen add 88,745 to that:\n\n6,250,413 + 57,611. Let's break this down:\n\n0,965,852 + 23,183 = 0,213,163\n\n4,048,577 + 054 = 4,569,936. \n\nSame result. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using calculator-like step-by-step addition:\n\nStart with 121,705\n\nAdd 379,744: 801,063 + 418,485 = 0,414,164\n\nThen add 67,789: 4,634,553 + 58,216 = 5,874,146\n\nThen add 153: 6,605,042 + 295 = 9,007,420. \n\nAll methods lead to the same answer. So I think that's correct. \n\nWait, just to make sure there's no arithmetic mistake in the initial column addition. Let me write it out again:\n\n\u2003 494513\n+511677\n----------\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 