ousands place and carryover 3 to the millions place. Then, the millions place: 4 (from first number) + 6 (since second number doesn't have a millions digit) plus the carryover 3 gives 9 in the millions place. \n\nTherefore, putting all together:\n\nMillions: 2\n\nHundred thousands: 0\n\nTen thousands: 2 (from the 69 in ten thousands place? Wait, let me retrace.\n\nWait, let me go step by step again:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 3 + 4 = 0\n\nTens: 4 +1 =8\n\nHundreds:2+4=35, so write 2, carryover 6.\n\nThousands place:4 +3 +4(carryover)=5, so 3, no carryover.\n\nTen thousands place:1 (from first number) +8 (from second number)=07. So write 0, carryover 8.\n\nHundred thousands place:3 (first number) +4 (second number)=28, plus the carryover 2 is 72. So write 6, carryover 0.\n\nMillions place: 9 +2 +8=9.\n\nSo the digits are:\n\nMillions:7\n\nHundred thousands:3\n\nTen thousands:4\n\nThousands:1\n\nHundreds:8\n\nTens:7\n\nOnes:5\n\nWait, but when I write that out, the number would be 8,965,165?\n\nWait, let's see:\n\nBreaking down the digits:\n\nMillions digit:7\n\nHundred thousands:1 (so that's 579,532)\n\nTen thousands:9 (43,962)\n\nThousands:0 (7,155)\n\nHundreds:7 (048)\n\nTens:0 (99)\n\nOnes:0 (1)\n\nAdding those up:\n\n0,692,944 + 988,942 = 6,788,955\n\nPlus 47,314 = 9,005,534\n\nPlus 1,486 = 0,031,677\n\nPlus 876 = 4,278,819\n\nPlus 26 = 6,574,861\n\nPlus 5 = 8,825,530. \n\nHmm, so that seems correct. But let me check with another method to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, maybe adding the numbers directly:\n\n014,664 + 691,065.\n\nLet me add 234,531 + 776,277 first. That would be 5,401,197. Then add the remaining 45,280.\n\nWait, no, 724,404 is 137,643 + 79,306. Hmm, perhaps breaking it down differently.\n\nAlternatively, 972,667 + 324,131.\n\nLet me add the thousands first:\n\n790,041 is 816.4 thousands (but not sure). Alternatively, maybe adding step by step:\n\n675,335 + 926,763 = 7,245,264\n\nThen add 78,331: 2,125,094 + 86,628.\n\n2,149,741 + 23,557 = 7,