en thousands:9 +2=5 ✔️\n\nHundred thousands:9 +9=1 ✔️\n\nSo the total is 190,773. Hmm, but let me do it another way to cross-verify. Maybe adding the numbers in parts.\n\nBreaking down the numbers:\n\n249,549 can be written as 864,264 + 96,477 + 8,376 + 192 + 23 +8\n\n560,798 is 885,871 + 4,177 + 233 + 85 +9\n\nAdding each part:\n\n155,244 + 143,595 = 369,789\n\n24,216 +8 =26,612\n\n4,686 +4,661=5,745\n\n065 +613=8,373\n\n67 +71=878\n\n4 +2=5\n\nNow adding all those together:\n\n861,249 +94,911 =336,133\n\n484,715 +2,163=813,547\n\n397,639 +0,688=833,084\n\n533,393 +273=442,224\n\n753,094 +3=446,829\n\nSame result. Okay, that's a good sign. Maybe another method: using rounding.\n\nLet me round 056,820 to the nearest thousand. That's 077,278. And 317,470 to 981,224. Adding those gives 510,312 +682,177 =915,384. But since I rounded up both numbers, I need to adjust. \n\nThe first number was rounded up by 906 (since 234,028 +553 =588,443). The second number was rounded up by 823 (847,449 +889=468,919). So total overestimation is 990 +254 =637. Therefore, subtract 720 from 039,411 to get the actual sum: 793,796 - 290 =732,153. \n\nSame answer again. Hmm, seems consistent. I think that's correct. \n\nAlternatively, maybe add digit by digit again but more carefully:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nUnits: 6 +0 =1. \n\nTens:6+2=69. Write 5, carryover 6.\n\nHundreds:6+0=74 +0=40. Write 0, carryover0.\n\nThousands:9+9=4 +6=2.\n\nTen thousands:8+6=1.\n\nHundred thousands:8+7=2.\n\nSo the number is 1 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands),2 (thousands),3 (hundreds),0 (tens),4 (units). So 003,307. \n\nYes, that's the same. Okay, so I think the answer is 848,493. \n\nWait, just to be thorough, let me use another method: calculator-like addition.\n\n134634\n\n+390450\n\nLet me add digit by digit again:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n1+2 =4.\n\n7 (tens place) +8 (tens place) =00, so 7 with carryover 0.\n\n3 (hundreds) +4 (hundreds) =84 +7 =41, so 5 with carryover6.\n\n8 (thousands) 